  "published": "2026-07-24T07:04:01.607Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Read scalability: shard locks move to parking_lot::RwLock, and TryGet(byte[], Span) now reads under the shard read lock with sampled LRU recency — a hit bumps recency ~1/8 of the time under a brief write lock instead of taking the write lock on every read. Concurrent TryGet throughput improves (~10-13% in a 4-core A/B, more with cores); single-thread is unchanged. Behavior note: TryGet's LRU recency is now approximate — use TryPeek to skip recency entirely. Object-returning reads (Get/GetString) keep exact LRU. Requires the 2.6.0 native binaries.",
